# apps/mobile/eas.json and .gitignore are hashed as raw file bytes by
# @expo/fingerprint (runtimeVersion policy "fingerprint"). Windows'
# core.autocrlf=true checks them out with CRLF, which differs from the LF
# bytes EAS's build environment uses — producing a fingerprint mismatch with
# no error anywhere (incident: 2026-09-18). Force LF so a Windows checkout's
# fingerprint can match a build's.
apps/mobile/eas.json text eol=lf
apps/mobile/.gitignore text eol=lf
